DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:20261019T115900Z
DTEND:20261019T125900Z
SUMMARY:[Information Retrieval & Search][Recommender Systems] WWW 2027 - Fu
 ll-paper abstract deadline
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: ACM Web Conference (formerly International Wo
 rld Wide Web Conference)\nWebsite: https://www2027.thewebconf.org/\nSourc
 e URL: https://www2027.thewebconf.org/research-track-papers/\nLocation: D
 ublin\, Ireland\nTopics: Information Retrieval & Search\, Recommender Sys
 tems\, Graphs & Graph Learning\, LLM Agents & Tool Use\nSize: XL\nSubmiss
 ion type: Paper-based\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-
 07\nNotes: Official homepage states full and short paper portals are open
 \; separate mandatory abstract gates. Research must substantively address
  the Web\, not merely use a web dataset. Preserve WWW as the stable serie
 s alias. Size is an editorial estimate.\nScope: Research on the Web as in
 frastructure and a socio-technical ecosystem. Characteristic ML-facing tr
 acks include search and recommendation\, retrieval-augmented and agentic 
 information access\, graph learning\, and semantic knowledge. Responsible
  Web and privacy research are substantive strands. Merely using a web dat
 aset or API is explicitly insufficient topical relevance.\nAdditional top
 ics: Knowledge Representation & Reasoning\, Data Mining & Data Science\, 
 Fairness & Responsible AI\, Privacy-preserving ML\, Ethics & Governance\n
 Scope sources (2027): https://www2027.thewebconf.org/research-track-paper
 s/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://www2027.thewebconf.org/research-track-papers/
END:VEVENT
